# 7. Eligibility Rules Engine

Build a reusable backend eligibility engine instead of scattering eligibility conditions throughout the frontend.

The engine should evaluate:
- Course
- Branch
- Specialization
- Graduation year
- 10th percentage
- 12th percentage
- CGPA / percentage
- Active backlogs
- Historical backlogs
- Any additional configured criteria

Return a structured result containing:
- Eligible / Not Eligible / Review Required
- Passed conditions
- Failed conditions
- Missing student information
- Human-readable explanation for every result

Use the same backend engine for:
- Student opportunity eligibility labels
- Application submission validation
- Admin applicant filters
- Eligible applicant counts
- Eligibility reports

The frontend must not be trusted to determine final eligibility.

Support percentage-based and CGPA-based criteria with explicit, institution-configured rules. Do not assume that CGPA and percentage are directly interchangeable.

If a rule requires missing information, return “Review Required” rather than making up a value.

Allow authorized Admins to configure a documented exception workflow. Any override must record the administrator, reason, timestamp, and previous result.

